[00:05.66]1. Jehovah is our refuge,
[00:11.32]Our God in whom we trust.
[00:22.56]His shadow is our shelter;
[00:27.56]Remain in it we must.
[00:32.56]His faithful ones he will defend,
[00:39.56]On this we know we can depend.
[00:44.56]Jehovah is a stronghold,
[00:50.68]Ever faithful, loyal, and just.
[01:05.47]2. Though thousands will have fallen
[01:16.12]And many at our side,
[01:19.79]The righteous and the meek ones
[01:23.46]Will never be denied.
[01:27.12]So in our hearts we need not fear;
[01:33.02]Calamity will not come near.
[01:41.02]From danger he will shield us,
[01:45.52]For beneath God’s wings we’ll reside.
[02:24.00]3. He’ll keep us and protect us
[02:29.00]From snares along our way,
[02:35.04]From terrors in the nighttime,
[02:40.54]And arrows by the day.
[02:46.46]Yes, there will be no cause for dread,
[02:51.98]No place where we will fear to tread.
[02:57.98]Jehovah is our refuge,
[03:03.34]Ever guarding us on our way.